*.xcodeproj/
.DS_Store
DerivedData/
build/

# Rust build artifacts — the bridge target dir is ~1.5GB of git deps + objects.
rust/**/target/

# The built xcframework: 112MB of static archive (2 slices x ~56MB), fully
# reproducible from scripts/build-xcframework.sh at a known crate sha. Git
# stores binaries whole and forever — committing it would add 112MB to every
# clone, permanently, for an artifact any Mac regenerates in ~5 minutes.
#
# What IS tracked is everything needed to produce it: the crate, its Cargo.lock,
# the rustc pin, the script, and the generated Swift bindings (so the app
# compiles even without a Rust toolchain — only LINKING needs the archive).
# The manifest inside each build records rustc/Xcode/SDK/ios-min/crate-sha, so
# two boxes' slices remain comparable without either being in git.
Frameworks/*.xcframework/
